.TH NEPLANG 1 "November 2026" "NepLang" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neplang \- run a NepLang program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neplang
[\fB\-\-vm\fR | \fB\-\-ir\fR | \fB\-\-emit\-c\fR | \fB\-\-build\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIout\fR]
.I file.np
[\fIargs\fR...]
.br
.B neplang
.BR run | check
.I file.np
.br
.B neplang build
.I file.np
.B \-o
.I out
.br
.B neplang
(starts the REPL)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B neplang
runs a program written in NepLang, a small programming language whose keywords are
romanized Nepali words mixed with English technical terms.
Source files must end in
.BR .np .
.PP
Each statement goes on its own line, and
.B #
starts a comment.
.SH LANGUAGE
.TP
.B vana(expr)
Print a value.
.TP
.B name = expr
Create or update a variable.
.B "x += 1"
(and
.BR "-= *= /= %=" )
is short for
.BR "x = x + 1" .
.TP
.B int x = 1   string? s   const MAX = 10
Declare a variable with a type
.RB ( int ", " float ", " bool ", " string ", " array ", " object ", " any
or a class or interface name);
.B ?
also allows
.BR khali .
A typed variable only accepts values of its type.
.B const
makes a constant.
.TP
.B yedi cond { } natara yedi cond { } natara { }
If / else-if / else.
.B natara
must be on the same line as the closing
.BR } .
.TP
.B jabasamma cond { }
While loop.
.TP
.B ko_lagi i in a..b { }
Count
.I i
from
.I a
up to, but not including,
.IR b .
.TP
.B kaam name(int a, b) int { farkau expr }
Define a function;
.B farkau
returns a value (without one, the result is
.BR khali ).
Parameter and return types are optional;
.B void
means the function gives nothing back.
.TP
.B ko_lagi x in arr { }
Loop over the items of an array, or the characters of a string.
.TP
.B [1, 2, 3]  a[i]  a[i] = v  lambai(a)
Arrays: literal, indexing from 0, item assignment, length.
.TP
.B \(dqNamaste \(dq + naam
Strings: double-quoted, with escapes
.BR \en ,
.BR \et ,
.B \e\(dq
and
.BR \e\e .
.B +
joins strings (a number on either side is turned into text);
.B s[i]
is the i-th character and
.B lambai(s)
the number of characters. Strings can't be changed in place.
.TP
.B class Name { field = 0 ... kaam method() { } }
Define a class. Create an object with
.BR Name(...) ,
which runs the method
.B banau
(the constructor) if there is one. Use
.B obj.field
and
.BR obj.method(...) .
Inside a method, bare field names refer to the current object, and
.B yo
is the object itself. Fields and methods whose names start with
.B _
are private to the class (and its parents and children).
.TP
.B class Kukur(Janawar, Bolne) { }   interface Bolne { kaam bolau() }
Inheritance: one parent class and any number of interfaces.
.B super.method(...)
calls the parent's method and
.B super(...)
in
.B banau
runs the parent's constructor. A class must define every method of its interfaces.
.TP
.B a.push(x)  s.upper()
Arrays and strings have methods (push pop insert remove clear contains index_of reverse
sort slice join copy sum min max length; upper lower trim split contains find replace
starts_with ends_with slice repeat chars code reverse length).
.PP
Values are whole numbers, decimal numbers (\fB3.14\fR), bools (\fBsacho\fR, \fBjutho\fR),
strings, arrays, objects and \fBkhali\fR (nothing). Comparisons
.B "== != < <= > >="
give sacho or jutho;
.BR ra ,
.B wa
and
.B hoina
are and, or and not. A condition must be a bool or a number (non-zero is true).
.PP
Built-in functions: lambai, thapa, hata, padha, sankhya, int, float, string, bool, prakar.
.SH MODES
With no option the program runs on the tree-walking interpreter. \fB\-\-vm\fR compiles it to bytecode and runs it on the virtual machine.
\fB\-\-ir\fR prints the optimized intermediate representation. \fB\-\-emit\-c\fR prints the generated C source.
\fB\-\-build\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIout\fR produces a native executable using the system C compiler (\fBCC\fR or \fBcc\fR).
\fBcheck\fR only reports errors. Every mode supports the whole language and prints the same output.
Arguments after the file are given to the program (\fBos.args()\fR).
With no file, \fBneplang\fR starts an interactive REPL: expressions are printed, and errors don't end the session.
.SH MODULES
\fBimport "file.np"\fR or \fBimport name\fR includes another file. Files are searched next to the importing file, then in the directories listed in \fBNEPLANG_PATH\fR.
\fBimport math\fR (and \fBstring\fR, \fBarray\fR, \fBio\fR, \fBtime\fR, \fBos\fR) enables a built-in standard-library module, used as \fBmath.sqrt(2)\fR.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
kaam factorial(n) {
    yedi n <= 1 {
        farkau 1
    }
    farkau n * factorial(n \- 1)
}
vana(factorial(6))
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a syntax, type or runtime error, which is printed with its file, line and
column (or the code given to \fBos.exit\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/charitraa/NepLang
